From: mscharged-port source integration
Subject: [PATCH] Restore original system aspect selection in the frontend diagnostic
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84
Classification: temporary diagnostic source selection; ordinary native/console code unchanged.

Admit the original SCGetAspectRatio/rlSetWidescreen block already present in
Initialize. It was excluded with unrelated debug and shadow prerequisites.
The native SC layer supplies the Wii system preference; original code still
selects its 640/854 projection and authored Credits slide. No text positions,
font requests, scrolling, game algorithms or source branches are changed.

diff --git a/src/Game/main.cpp b/src/Game/main.cpp
index 44070fe..f2a9750 100644
--- a/src/Game/main.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/main.cpp
@@ -679,12 +679,16 @@ static void Initialize()
     ModeledScreenTransition::s_3DView = GetLayerView(eCLV_Transitions3D);
     SetDebugFontView(GetLayerView(eCLV_Debug));
     SetDebugSquareView(GetLayerView(eCLV_DebugSquare));
+#endif // unrelated world/debug view prerequisites
+#if !defined(MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_MAIN_BOOTSTRAP) || defined(MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_MAIN_FRONTEND)
     bool widescreen = true;
     if (SCGetAspectRatio() != 1)
     {
         widescreen = false;
     }
     rlSetWidescreen(widescreen);
+#endif // original system aspect selects the frontend projection and slide
+#if !defined(MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_MAIN_BOOTSTRAP)
     g_ShapeRenderer.Initialize(resourcePool);
     g_ShapeRenderer.m_eView = GetLayerView(eCLV_Characters);
     InitMaxProjectedShadows();
